  "final_message": "Done. The todo app is complete and verified:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): Flask + SQLite (`./data/app.db`, created on startup). Bearer-token auth (PBKDF2 hashes, register/login/logout), full CRUD with per-user isolation (other users' todos return 404), paged list sorted open\u2192due date (nulls last)\u2192newest, `completed_at` set/cleared automatically, validation messages from the API surfaced as `{\"error\": ...}`.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`): React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind v4 (via `@tailwindcss/vite`, only `src/index.css` imports Tailwind). Auth screen, header with username/open-todo counter/sign-out, add form, inline editing, immediate-save checkbox, delete confirmation, all/open/completed tabs, priority filter, overdue highlighting, \"Load more\".\n\n**Dockerfile fix**: the pinned install (`pip -r -c --hashes`) failed because `requirements.txt` lacked hashes; regenerated it with all transitive deps pinned and hashed from `requirements.lock` \u2014 verified `pip install -r requirements.txt -c requirements.lock` now succeeds, along with `npm ci` and `npm run build`.\n\nAll 40 API assertions pass, TS typecheck is clean, and a gunicorn smoke test on port-same-as-docker confirmed health, static serving, SPA fallback, and data persistence across restart.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
